para(f'At least {observed_restarts} PCB restarts were observed during experimental comparisons. Their cause is unresolved: no USB reset-reason capture was available. The mixed 57 GHz window and interrupted CFAR windows are excluded from stable-profile tables, with raw evidence retained. This is a stability limitation, not proof that a particular command caused the restarts.')
para('Capture instrumentation revision 1 performed synchronous status checks in the receive loop, creating some local collector gaps. Revisions 2 and 3 poll health asynchronously. Revision 3 also preserves interrupted files and aborts a comparison after 30 seconds without new fresh frames. Receive gaps in early windows therefore cannot be attributed solely to GCP loss. A missing health response is not treated as a reboot. Radar boot IDs and known frame counter decreases are checked separately.')
para('Command acknowledgement and numeric read-back are distinct. Frame, mode, Doppler FFT, range, clutter and CFAR replies are retained; a frequency or velocity acknowledgement alone does not independently measure the emitted waveform. Getter replies are collected during application before start; fresh frames are verified after start. Settings are not independently re-queried over UART mid-window. Literal CFAR 1 80 reads back SNR 24 on this firmware, so it is not interpreted as a linear threshold of 80.')
failures=comparison.get('failures',[])
if failures:
 for f in failures:para(f"{f['label']}: {f['error']}")
else:para('No rejected profile is recorded in completed comparison metadata so far. In-progress operations are not represented by that statement.')
para('Capture-complete marker: '+('present' if finished else 'not present')+'. Original-profile restoration: '+str(completion.get('baseline_restored','not yet due / not verified'))+'.')
h('What the results cannot establish')
for text in ['A validated two-person count, sleeping state, breathing or vital signs.','False-positive rate without an empty-bed test; false-negative rate without synchronized annotations.','Full body height while lying down; observed point height is posture-dependent.','Performance in another room, mounting, bedding arrangement or body position.','Fall-detection performance: the current fall prototype is single-person, and no deliberate fall trial was performed.']:para(text)
h('Next controlled validation')
for text in [
 'Measure the actual bed width, length and mattress-top height; verify the physical antenna rotation and mounting before changing dashboard coordinates.',
 'After the room is empty, collect an empty-bed control, then one person on each side and both people together with synchronized notes. Include lying still, rolling over and sitting up. Use these labels to distinguish merging from false furniture groups.',
 'Do not interpret the suggested 114-degree heading and 26-31-degree tilt as a verified optimum. They are calculated aiming directions for the assumed bed. A physical aiming comparison requires repeating the same labeled controls.',
 'Capture USB boot/reset logs before resuming aggressive hardware sweeps. The observed restarts remain unexplained. Keep the original working profile available for immediate recovery.',
 'Run any noise-baseline command only when the sensing area is actually empty and still; no such calibration was performed with the occupied bed tonight.',
 'Save a startup profile only after a repeatable labeled comparison confirms it. This experiment left the original startup profile unchanged.'
]:para(text)
h('Reproducibility and rollback')
para('Evidence folder: output/radar_overnight_20261125. baseline.json preserves the original active and saved profiles. events.jsonl records all requested profiles and complete command replies. Each completed segment has a JSON summary, compressed processed-point packet archive and per-frame metric archive. replay-analysis.json and profile-summary.json contain independent offline results. No access keys are included in this report.')
para('Source: Sameer856/citraverse-v2, branch codex/radar-dashboard-room, tools/radar_overnight. Dashboard rollback milestones: dashboard-v1.0.0 (before bed), dashboard-v1.1.0 (bed layout), dashboard-v1.2.0 (experimental bed groups), dashboard-v1.2.1 (bounded display continuity). Restore source with a new revert commit and redeploy; checking out a Git tag alone does not change the live Site.')
if deployment:
 para('Dashboard publication: '+str(deployment.get('status','unknown'))+'; version '+str(deployment.get('version','unknown'))+'; source '+str(deployment.get('commit_sha','unknown'))+'. '+str(deployment.get('url','')),'SmallCustom')
 para('Dashboard verification: '+str(deployment.get('verification','not recorded')),'SmallCustom')
