data={'finished':finished,'generated':now,'manifest':manifest,'summary':summary,'segments':segments,'replay':replay,'recommendation':recommendation,'completion':completion,'ranking':ranking,'temporal':temporal,'aim':aim,'runtime':runtime,'frozen':frozen,'suspension':suspension,'crossover':crossover,'crossover_evaluation':crossover_evaluation,'crossover_criteria':crossover_criteria,'density_runtime':density_runtime,'density_frozen':density_frozen,'observed_restarts':observed_restarts,'display_runtime':display_runtime,'software_evaluation':software_evaluation,'final_selection':final_selection,'holdout':holdout}
# Omit device health and long transcript objects from the visual payload.
for s in data['segments']:s.pop('health_before',None);s.pop('health_after',None)
data['temporal']={'version':temporal.get('version')}
data['replay']={'segments':[{'segment':r['segment'],'sampled_seconds':r['sampled_seconds'],'cluster_fractions':{k:v for k,v in r['cluster_fractions'].items() if k.startswith('r') or k.startswith('room3d')}} for r in replay.get('segments',[])]}
canvas='''import {Stack,H1,H2,Text,Grid,Stat,Table,Divider,Select,useCanvasState,useHostTheme} from 'cursor/canvas';
const data:any=__DATA__;
const pct=(v:number)=>`${(100*v).toFixed(1)}%`;
export default function RadarOvernight(){const {tokens:t}=useHostTheme();const [radius,setRadius]=useCanvasState('radar-radius','r0.4-min3');const [bedWidth,setBedWidth]=useCanvasState('aim-bed-width','1');const rows=data.summary.profiles||[];const replay=new Map(data.replay.segments.map((s:any)=>[s.segment,s]));return <Stack gap={20}><H1>Citraverse overnight radar experiment</H1><Text tone="secondary">{data.finished?'Capture complete':'DRAFT — capture still running'} · {data.generated}</Text><Text>{data.recommendation.conclusion||'No final recommendation yet. Compare the completed windows below.'}</Text><Grid columns={3} gap={16}><Stat label="Final holdout" value={`${(data.holdout.minutes||0).toFixed(1)} min`}/><Stat label="Fresh radar rate" value={data.holdout.metrics?`${data.holdout.metrics.fresh_fps.toFixed(2)} FPS`:'Pending'}/><Stat label="Two recent groups · proxy" value={data.holdout.metrics?pct(data.holdout.metrics.two_recent_fraction):'Pending'}/></Grid><Text tone="secondary">All stages: {data.segments.length} complete windows · {(data.segments.reduce((n:number,s:any)=>n+s.duration_s,0)/60).toFixed(1)} recorded minutes · {data.segments.reduce((n:number,s:any)=>n+(s.counts.fresh||0),0).toLocaleString()} fresh frames.</Text><Text tone="secondary">User reports two people remain in bed. Two clusters are a spatial proxy, not verified person-count accuracy. Exact bed dimensions remain unconfirmed.</Text><H2>Final active settings</H2><Table headers={['Radar command','Setting']} rows={data.recommendation.profile?(()=>{const p=data.recommendation.profile;return [['mmwc freq',String(p.frequency)],['mmwc range',`${p.range_mm} ${p.resolution_mm}`],['mmwc veloc',`${p.speed_mm_s} ${p.speed_step_mm_s}`],['mmwc frame',`${p.frame_ms} 0`],['mmwc cfar',`${p.static_rm} ${p.cfar_value}`+(p.cfar_method>=0?` ${p.cfar_method}`:' (two arguments)')],['mmwc clutter_rm',String(p.clutter_rm)],['Fixed output','comtype 1 · mode 4 2 · dop_fft 1 · coord cart · report points 0']]})():[]}/><Text tone="secondary">{data.recommendation.cfar_readback||'Final live read-back is pending.'}</Text><Divider/><H2>Profile comparison</H2><Table headers={['Profile','Minutes','Fresh FPS','Bed support','Both halves','Outside points','Max segment P95 age']} rows={rows.map((p:any)=>[p.labels[0],p.duration_minutes.toFixed(1),p.fresh_fps.toFixed(2),pct(p.bed_presence_fraction),pct(p.both_halves_fraction),pct(p.outside_point_fraction),`${p.age_p95_segment_max} ms`])}/><H2>Controlled static-return repeat</H2><Text>The bounded comparison changes only static removal: baseline → two alternate windows → baseline. Its gates were recorded before alternate capture. They evaluate transport and grouping proxies, not verified person detection.</Text><Text>Evaluation: {data.crossover_evaluation.status||'pending'}{data.crossover_evaluation.status==='evaluated'?` · alternate passed all gates: ${data.crossover_evaluation.alternate_passed}`:''}</Text><Table headers={['Method','Baseline: two recent','Alternate: two recent','Change','Baseline: more than two','Alternate: more than two']} rows={Object.entries(data.crossover_evaluation.aggregate||{}).map(([method,v]:[string,any])=>[method,pct(v.two.baseline),pct(v.two.alternate),`${(100*v.two.difference).toFixed(1)} points`,pct(v.many.baseline),pct(v.many.alternate)])}/><H2>Exploratory spatial comparison</H2><Select value={radius} onChange={setRadius} options={['r0.2-min3','r0.2-min6','r0.3-min3','r0.3-min6','r0.4-min3','r0.4-min6','r0.5-min3','r0.5-min6','r0.65-min3','r0.65-min6'].map(v=>({value:v,label:v.replace('r','Radius ').replace('-min',' m / minimum ')+' points'}))}/><Table headers={['Window','Samples','Room 3D: 2 clusters','Bed: 1','Bed: 2','Bed: >2']} rows={data.segments.map((s:any)=>{const r:any=replay.get(s.segment);const f=r?.cluster_fractions||{};return [s.segment,r?.sampled_seconds||0,pct(f['room3d-two']||0),pct(f[radius+'-one']||0),pct(f[radius+'-two']||0),pct(f[radius+'-many']||0)]})}/><Text tone="secondary">Horizontal bed clustering avoids splitting a body by height; smaller radii may fragment it. Neither method recognizes identity. The replay samples one fresh frame per receive-second.</Text><Divider/><H2>Frozen bed-grouping validation</H2><Text>Across-bed 0.15 m; along-bed 1 m; 200 ms fresh evidence; minimum three distinct positions. No forced person count. Only complete baseline windows starting after the method freeze count as prospective.</Text><Table headers={['Window','Role','Room: two','Bed: two recent','Bed: more than two','Bed: none']} rows={(data.runtime.segments||[]).map((r:any)=>[r.segment,r.role||(r.validation?'Prospective':'Pre-freeze'),pct(r.room_two_fraction),pct(r.bed_two_recent_fraction),pct(r.bed_more_than_two_recent_fraction),pct(r.bed_zero_recent_fraction)])}/><H2>Separate density candidate</H2><Text>The later candidate uses 0.12 m across-bed, 0.8 m along-bed, a one-second position history and six-neighbour density cores. Three distinct positions must still refresh within 200 ms to count as recent. Its development windows are 000, 003, 008 and 009; only later complete windows qualify as prospective.</Text><Table headers={['Window','Density role','Earlier: two recent','Density: two recent','Density: more than two','Any weak group']} rows={(data.density_runtime.segments||[]).map((r:any)=>{const prior=(data.runtime.segments||[]).find((s:any)=>s.segment===r.segment);return [r.segment,r.role,pct(prior?.bed_two_recent_fraction||0),pct(r.bed_two_recent_fraction),pct(r.bed_more_than_two_recent_fraction),pct(r.has_weak_evidence_fraction)]})}/><Text tone="secondary">Position history can smooth geometry for up to one second; weak historical groups do not count as current detections. Reduced fragmentation can coexist with longer merged-group runs.</Text><H2>Display continuity</H2><Text>Small index losses can preserve display tracks within a bounded source/receive interval. Stale frames and long gaps still clear them. Fall continuity stays strict. Raw missing frames remain missing.</Text><Table headers={['Window','Role','Strict display resets','Bounded display resets']} rows={(data.display_runtime.segments||[]).map((r:any)=>[r.segment,r.role,r.strict_display_resets,r.tolerant_display_resets])}/><H2>Final candidate and holdout</H2><Text>Software-selection status: {data.software_evaluation.status||'pending'}. Final candidate: {data.final_selection.selected_method||'not frozen yet'}; display policy: {data.final_selection.display_policy||'pending'}.</Text><Text>Independent final windows: {data.holdout.completed_windows||0} · {(data.holdout.minutes||0).toFixed(1)} minutes. Two-group fractions remain unverified person-count proxies.</Text><H2>Missing and merged groups</H2><Table headers={['Window','One recent group','Longest zero run','Longest below-two run']} rows={(data.runtime.segments||[]).map((r:any)=>[r.segment,pct(r.bed_one_recent_fraction||0),r.longest_zero_recent_sample_run??'—',r.longest_under_two_recent_sample_run??'—'])}/><Text tone="secondary">Runs count consecutive roughly one-second samples; they are not precisely timed outages or verified missed people.</Text><H2>Failures and recovery</H2><Text>At least {data.observed_restarts} PCB restarts were observed; aggressive parameter sweeps were halted. Cause remains unresolved. Interrupted and mixed-profile windows are excluded from stable rankings. A bounded repeat of a previously successful static-return setting, if run, is reported separately. No occupied-room noise calibration was run.</Text><Text>Early synchronous telemetry polls caused some collector gaps; revised polling runs asynchronously. A receive gap alone is not evidence of GCP dropping a frame.</Text><H2>Recorded setup</H2><Text>3 × 3 × 3 m room; sensor at far-left, height 2 m, 180° roll, 10° down tilt, 135° heading. Bed at far-right toward near-right; initial assumed size 1 × 2 m, 0.55 m high, 0.15 m wall gap.</Text><H2>Calculated physical aiming guide</H2><Text>Choose an assumed bed width to inspect the geometry. The room and mounting values come from the supplied screenshots; the bed dimensions are still unconfirmed.</Text><Select value={bedWidth} onChange={setBedWidth} options={['1','1.5','1.8','2'].map(v=>({value:v,label:`Assumed bed width ${v} m`}))}/><svg viewBox="0 0 320 215" role="img" aria-label="Plan view comparing the current room-centre direction with the calculated bed-centre direction" style={{width:'100%',maxWidth:480,color:t.text.primary}}><rect x="10" y="10" width="180" height="180" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" opacity="0.5"/><rect x={181-60*Number(bedWidth)} y="19" width={60*Number(bedWidth)} height="120" fill="currentColor" fillOpacity="0.08" stroke="currentColor"/><line x1="19" y1="19" x2="100" y2="100" stroke="currentColor" strokeWidth="2"/><line x1="19" y1="19" x2={181-30*Number(bedWidth)} y2="79" stroke="currentColor" strokeWidth="2" strokeDasharray="4 3"/><circle cx="19" cy="19" r="4" fill="currentColor"/><circle cx={181-30*Number(bedWidth)} cy="79" r="3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"/><text x="208" y="35" fill="currentColor" fontSize="13">3 × 3 m room</text><text x="208" y="65" fill="currentColor" fontSize="13">Solid: current</text><text x="208" y="90" fill="currentColor" fontSize="13">Dashed: guide</text><text x="10" y="208" fill="currentColor" fontSize="13">Near wall · bed head at far-right</text></svg><Table headers={['Target height above floor','Calculated heading','Calculated down tilt','Slant range']} rows={(data.aim.scenarios||[]).filter((s:any)=>s.assumed_bed_width_m===Number(bedWidth)).map((s:any)=>[`${s.target_height_m.toFixed(2)} m`,`${s.heading_to_target_deg.toFixed(1)}°`,`${s.down_tilt_to_target_deg.toFixed(1)}°`,`${s.slant_range_m.toFixed(2)} m`])}/><Text tone="secondary">This is a calculated direction, not a measured antenna field of view. Physically check the mounting before changing coordinates. A dashboard rotation does not steer the antenna.</Text><H2>Evidence and limits</H2><Text>Every temporary profile is checked against the radar's reply and fresh frames. No firmware flash, occupied-room noise calibration or NVS save is part of this experiment. Original startup settings remain recoverable.</Text><Text>Without empty-bed and one-person controls, persistent furniture returns cannot be distinguished conclusively from sleepers. Full standing height, breathing, sleep state and fall accuracy are outside this test.</Text><Text tone="secondary">Local evidence: output/radar_overnight_20261125. GitHub: Sameer856/citraverse-v2 → codex/radar-dashboard-room → tools/radar_overnight.</Text></Stack>}
'''.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data,separators=(',',':')))
